    "Only unannotated phantom source datatype positions may refine to Region, from scoped Region actuals at the exact defining nominal argument position.",
    "Explicit source annotations, runtime constructor fields and imported interface parameter kinds remain authoritative. Client signatures and qualified aliases cannot rekind producer declarations.",
    "Class methods retain their actual global symbol and enclosing parameter forall context. Nested type binders preserve lexical scope and the existing shadowing refusal.",
    "Strict inferred generalization requires a syntactic value with empty performed effects, retaining existing captured/literal-meta restrictions. Applications and ordinary annotations remain monomorphic; function values may carry latent effects.",
    "A direct explicit forall annotation in a strict RHS retains a checked CPolyIntro/UForall with pure construction. Its declared contract is instantiated at use, without inferred generalization of an evaluated mutable allocation."
